## Privacy RED against prior follower-only predicates

Command (cwd: nest-backend):
`npm run test:e2e -- --runTestsByPath test/e2e/story-audience.e2e-spec.ts -t "allows either connection direction and revokes only after the final edge is lost"`

Expected before implementation: owner-following-only member is absent from candidates.
Actual: failed on the real HTTP candidate response; expected friend and follower IDs, received only friend ID. 1 failed, 3 skipped; exit 1. Only the prior safety-list candidate/add predicates were temporarily reinstated for this reproduction and then restored.

## Throttler fixture diagnosis (before test-fixture isolation)

Command (cwd: nest-backend):
`npm run test:e2e -- --runTestsByPath test/e2e/story-audience.e2e-spec.ts`

Expected before fixture correction: all four E2E cases pass.
Actual: case 4 failed when HTTP `GET /stories` returned 429 with body `{"success":false,"error":{"code":"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR","message":"ThrottlerException: Too Many Requests"},"requestId":null,"timestamp":"2026-09-30T05:40:31.644Z","path":"/stories"}`; cases 1–3 passed; exit 1. Source tracing identified the route-specific default short bucket (10 hits / 1 second / client IP) accumulating calls from prior test cases. Production throttle was unchanged.

